@Node Desc

zmf.library/--description--

   NAME
      zmf.library

   DESC
      This library is a support library for Zeus. It is not the same
      as the zeus.library, it contains totally different functions.
      This library supports the FileControl and MsgControl programs, and is the
      interface to enable programmers to access the functions these offer.

      All the FILE FUNCTIONS require FileControl to be running.
      All the MSG FUNCTIONS require MsgControl to be running.
      ALL functions require Zeus to be active.

   USAGE
      This library is the same as any other shared library you may have
      used in the past.

      Zmf uses the library base name of PipeUtilBase.  This will change in
      the future to ZMFBase but PipeUtilBase will remain supported.


      /* C Include Files */

         clib/zmf_protos.h              - This contains the C prototyping
                                          for the functions in the lib.
         pragmas/zmf_pragmas.h          - This is for compilers that
                                          support #pragma calls, and work
                                          out the library offsets from that.
                                          (SAS in particular)
         libraries/zmf.h                - This contains structure definition
                                          and #define info to support the
                                          library functions.
         proto/zmf.h                    - This loads all the include files,
                                          and set's up an extern to the
                                          PipeUtilBase. Mostly, you should
                                          just include this file.
      /* ASM Files */

         libraries/zmf.i                - As libraries/zmf.h but for
                                          68k assembler interpreters.
         libraries/zmf_lib.i            - Containing LVO offsets for the
                                          functions in the library.

      /* Generic Files */

         zmf.fd                         - The function descriptor file for
                                          all the functions, in standard
                                          Developer format.

   EXAMPLE

         ------------------- 8< --------------------

         /* Runnable Example */

         #include <proto/zmf.h>

         struct Library *PipeUtilBase;

         void main ( int argc, char **argv )
         {
            char buffer [] = "make this string uppercase!";

            /* open library */
            if ( ! ( PipeUtilBase = OpenLibrary ( "zmf.library", 0 ) ) )
            {
               /* Library did not open */
               puts ( "Can't Open Library...\n" ) ;
               return;
            }

            printf ( "Buffer Before = \"%s\"\n", buffer ) ;
            /* Call library function */
            MakeUpper ( buffer, strlen ( buffer ) ) ;
            printf ( "Buffer After = \"%s\"\n", buffer ) ;
            /* Close the pipeutil library */
            CloseLibrary ( PipeUtilBase ) ;
         }

         ------------------- 8< --------------------
            

   SEE ALSO
      Your compilers manual.

@EndNode      

