@Node MySort()

zmf.library/MySort

    NAME
      MySort - Useful List Sort Routine

    SYNOPSIS
      MySort ( List, Function )
                A0    A1

      void MySort ( struct List *, int (*)(struct Node *, struct Node *) )

    FUNCTION
      Sort (in place) a list using any structure reference.

      The sorting is performed by a mergesort, and is of O(N log N).
      This is as fast as you can realistically make a generic linked list
      sort routine.

      To sort a list of nodes using the ln_Name field of the Node
      structure, also see zeus.library/SortList().

    INPUTS
      List --     'struct List *' or 'struct MinList *' to sort.
      Function -- A Pointer to a function which returns a result in the
                  style of 'strcmp'. See Example for more details. NB; 
                  This function must use the '__saveds' keyword in SAS C
                  to preserve the registers.

                  The Function should return
                   <0 - If the 1st comparison (struct Node *First) is below
                         the Second (struct Node *Second).
                    0 - If the expressions match.
                   >0 - If the 1st comparison is above the second.

                  This means you can also sort numerically.
    RESULTS
      None.

    EXAMPLES
      ------------------- 8< --------------------

         int __saveds
         SortFunction ( struct MyNode *First, struct MyNode *Second )
         {
            return ( 
               stricmp ( First->Name, Second->Name )
               ) ;
         }

         int __saveds
         NumSortFunction ( struct MyNode *First, struct MyNode *Second )
         {
            if ( First->Number < Second->Number )
               return ( 1 ) ;
            if ( First->Number > Second->Number )
               return ( -1 ) ;
            return ( 0 ) ;
            /* OR: More Simply -
                 return ( First->Number - Second->Number ) ;
             */
         }

         void main ( void )
         {
            struct   List   *ListToSort;

            /* Sort alphabetically */
            MySort ( ListToSort, SortFunction ) ;
            /* sort numerically */
            MySort ( ListToSort, NumSortFunction ) ;
         }

      ------------------- 8< --------------------

@EndNode

