@Node InitParse()

zmf.library/InitParse

   NAME
      InitParse - Init Structure for use with ParseNum and ParseChar

   SYNOPSIS
      void InitParse ( ParseKey, ParseString )
       D0               A0          A1

           InitParse ( struct parsekey *, char * )

   FUNCTION
      Provides a way to handle number ranges as used in numerous
      Zeus programs such as mbManager, or with ParseChar to handle
      multiple items in a string.

   INPUTS
      ParseKey - An allocated 'parsekey' structure.
      ParseString - A Character Pointer to the String to Pass

   EXAMPLE

      -----------------------
      #include <proto/zmf.h>

      struct parsekey    Key;
      char            String[] = "1-3,7,8,200,30-40";

      InitParse ( &Key, (char *) &String ) ;
      -----------------------

   RESULT
      None

   SEE ALSO
         @{"ParseNum" Link ParseNum()}, @{"ParseChar" Link ParseChar()}

@EndNode

@Node ParseNum()

zmf.library/ParseNum

   NAME
      ParseNum - Useful Routine for Parsing Number Strings.

   SYNOPSIS
      ParseNum   ( Key, Function, Arg2 ) 
                    A0   A1        D0
       
      void ParseNum   ( struct parsekey *, (int) (*)(ULONG, ULONG), ULONG )

   FUNCTION
      Provides a way to handle number ranges as used in numerous
      Zeus programs such as mbManager.

   INPUTS
      ParseKey - Structure initaliazed by InitParse
      Function - Callback function to call for every number in string.
      Arg2    - Second Argument for 'Function'.

   EXAMPLE

      -----------------------
      #include <proto/plsupport.h>

      void main ( int argc, char **argv )
      {
         struct parsekey    Key;
         char            String[] = "1-3,7,8,200,30-40";
         int              PrintNum ( ULONG, ULONG ) ;

         InitParse ( &Key, (char *) &String ) ;

         ParseNum ( &Key, PrintNum, 0L ) ;
      }

      int __saveds
      ParseNum ( ULONG Number, ULONG SecondArg )
      {
         printf ( "Got A Number = %ld\n", Number ) ;

         /* Return 0 if you want ParseNum to Quit */
         return ( 1 ) ;
      }
      -----------------------

   RESULT
      None

@EndNode

@Node ParseChar()

zeus.library/ParseChar

   NAME
      ParseChar - Useful Routine for Parsing Char Strings.

   SYNOPSIS
      void ParseChar   ( Key, Function, Arg2 ) 
       D0        A0      A1      D0
       
      void ParseChar   ( struct parsekey *, (int) (*)(ULONG, ULONG), ULONG )

   FUNCTION
      As used in, e.g., tagging files on the BBS, this allows you
      to run a function on each of the items/words present in a
      string.

   INPUTS
      ParseKey - Structure initaliazed by InitParse
      Function - Callback function to call for every file in string.
      Arg2    - Second Argument for 'Function'.

   EXAMPLE

      -----------------------
      #include <proto/plsupport.h>

      void main ( int argc, char **argv )
      {

         struct parsekey    Key;
         char               String[] = "File1 File2 File3 File4";
         int                 PrintChar ( ULONG, ULONG ) ;

         InitParse ( &Key, (char *) &String ) ;

         ParseChar ( &Key, PrintChar, 0L ) ;

      }

      int __saveds PrintChar ( char *String, ULONG SecondArg )
      {
         printf ( "Got A String = %ld\n", String ) ;

         /* Return 0 if you want ParseChar to Quit */
         return ( 1 ) ;
      }
      -----------------------

    RESULT
      None

    SEE ALSO
   @{"InitParse" Link InitParse()}

@EndNode

