@Node LoadFile()

zmf.library/LoadFile

   NAME
      LoadFile   

   SYNOPSIS
      FullFile = LoadFile ( Number, Flags )
       d0                    d0      d1

      struct fullFile *LoadFile ( ULONG, ULONG )

   FUNCTION
      Returns the file data structure of a certain file, as defined
      in the includes with "fullfile".

   INPUTS
      Number - File Number to load. You can use FileNameToNumber
               to get this if you don't know it.
      Flags  - 
               LF_DESCRIPTION - Loads the files description into
               FullFile->ff_text. This should be FreeMem'ed
               by you, the size will be FullFile->ff_file->DescLength + 1
               LF_LOADDELETED - Loads files retained in catalogue,
               although marked deleted.

   RESULTS
      >0 - A struct fullFile pointer to the file required.
       0 - Failure (File doesn't exist).

   NOTES
      ***************
      You must free all the data structures yourself. See example.
      ***************

   EXAMPLE
      
      ------------------- 8< --------------------
      struct fullFile *file;

      file = LoadFile ( 5, LF_DESCRIPTION ) ;
      if ( file )
      {
         printf ( "FileName = %s", file->ff_file->FileName ) ;

         FreeMem ( file->ff_file, sizeof ( struct file ) ) ;
         FreeMem ( file->ff_text, strlen ( file->ff_text ) + 1 ) ;
         FreeMem ( file, sizeof ( struct fullFile ) ) ;
      }
      ------------------- 8< --------------------

    BUGS

@EndNode

@Node EditFile()

zmf.library/EditFile

    NAME
      EditFile

    SYNOPSIS
      signed int ( struct file *EditFile, UBYTE *Text )
       d0           a0                      a1

    FUNCTION
      Edit's a file record, and a files' description. 

      NB: You are not allowed to edit the file's name or
      number record. This function should be used mainly for
      updating the "Number of Downloads" fields, and the
      validation flags. Due to the excessive amount of
      work required in updating indexes, if you wish to 
      change the files name, you should call DeleteCatFile,
      and then re-save the file.

    INPUTS
      EditFile - Fully Completed record of file to edit.
                 Do not edit the Number, FileName, DescLength, DescPos,
                 AlphaPosNext and AlphaPosPrev fields!

      Text -     New Description for file, or NULL if the file description
                 is to stay unchanged.

    RESULTS
      1 - Successful!
      0 - PLFILE not Running!
      -1- Bad Args!
      -2- Cannot open Description File
      -3- Cannot write new Description
      -4- Cannot open Data File
      -5- Cannot write new Record

    NOTES
      There isn't any error checking, and it will write out whatever you
       specify in 'EditFile', so WATCH OUT!. If you are deleting a file,
       use DeleteCatFile instead.

    BUGS

@EndNode

@Node SaveFile()

zmf.library/SaveFile

    NAME
        SaveFile -- Saves a file into the Zeus catalogue.

    SYNOPSIS
        SaveFile ( struct savefile *File, ULONG Flags )
                    a0                     d0

    FUNCTION
        Adds a file into the Zeus catalogue, allowing the system
        to access the file in User file listings, FileEd
        program, and available to the other file functions in the
        library such as LoadFile and ScanFiles.

        You are required to have copied the file, the name of which
        should be supplied in File->filename, into one of the directories
        which the file areas path field points to. SaveFile will
        check that the file exists, and retrieve its size.

        If an error occurs during the saving of the file, a transaction
        file will have been created in the Zeus File Directory
        named FILETRANSACTION-<number>, where number is the datestamp
        of when the file is saved. If this is present when FileControl is
        next loaded, then the user will be informed, and steps should
        be taken (such as calling FileRebuild) to repair the filebase.

    INPUTS
        SaveFile --
            area -- number of area to save in.
            filename -- name of physical file to save.
            desc -- character pointer to file description.
            flags -- 
                #define FI_UNVALIDATED (ULONG) 0x0001
                #define FI_FREEFILE (ULONG) 0x0002
                #define FI_DELETED (ULONG) 0x0004
                #define FI_OFFLINE (ULONG) 0x0008
            yesnoFakeInfo -- not implemented.
            fakeinfo -- not implemented.
            UserName -- uploader of the file (e.g. "SysOp")

        Flags -- as yet unused.

    RESULTS
        0  -- OK (File Saved).
        -1 -- No Such Area Number
        -2 -- Couldn't access physical file.
        -3 -- File already in catalogue.
        -4 -- No Description Supplied.
        -5 -- Invalid Filename (first character should be alpha-
              numerical)
        -6 -- Couldn't open File Description file.
        -7 -- Couldn't open File Data file.
        -8 -- As -5 (File Catalogue may need rebuilding).
        -9 -- Couldn't open Index File.

    BUGS

@EndNode

