@Node LoadMessage()

zmf.library/LoadMessage

   NAME
      LoadMessage -- Load a single message from system.

   SYNOPSIS
      struct WholeMessage *LoadMessage ( int, ULONG, ULONG )
       D0                                 D0   D1     D2
      msg = LoadMessage ( Area, Number, Flags )

   FUNCTION
      Load's a Local/Netmail/EchoMail or UUCP Message from the system.
      The Message Text will be in standard FidoNet format. Ignore all
      soft returns (0x0A's). 0x0D lines are for paragraph markers.
      All text should be real-time line wrapped. Use
      zmf.library/LineWrap().
   
   INPUTS
      Area   -- Message Area this message belongs to.
      Number -- Message Number
      Flags  -- Set to LM_NOFIDOINFO if you do not require FidoNet
                control lines to be included in the text, otherwise NULL.
                LM_NEXTMSG -- If the message required has been deleted,
                skip to the next available message (within Pointer
                boundaries). The number returned can be retreived
                from msg->wm_Msg.Number.

   RESULTS
      0 - Error/Message not found
      >0- Pointer to Data 

   BUGS

@EndNode

@Node SaveMessage()

zmf.library/SaveMessage

   NAME
      SaveMessage

   SYNOPSIS
      signed int SaveMessage ( struct WriteMsgStruct *wms )
       d0                       a0

   FUNCTION
      Saves a Message according to the data in 'wms'.

   INPUTS
      wms - A pointer to a WriteMsgStruct structure. The fields are -

         From         - Who sent this message.

         To           - Who this message is addressed to (or ALL)

         Subject      - The topic of this message

         FromAddress  - Structure containing information about where
                        the message originated from. Find out from
                        the function 'GetMsgAreaData'.

         ToAddress    - Structure containing information about where
                        the message is going to. If this is an
                        EchoMail area, then you need not worry about
                        these fields, simply initalise them all to
                        '0'.

         ReplyTo      - If this Message is a reply to another message,
                        put the number of the original message in here,
                        or '0' if this message is not part of a thread.

         Flags        - Message Flags -

                        Please see includes!

                        MI_PRIVATE            0x0001
                        MI_FILEATTACHED       0x0002 ; Never in Echomail areas
                        MI_REPLY              0x0004 ; Then set ReplyTo
                        MI_DELETED            0x0008 ; Never set this!
                        MI_SENDERANONYMOUS    0x0010 ; But still set 'From'
                        MI_RECEIVEANONYMOUS   0x0020 ; But still set 'To'
                        MI_DELETEUPONRECEIVE  0x0040 ; Usually not in Echomail areas

         MessageArea - Area Number to place message.

         Text         - unsigned char pointer to the message text (you can
                        have a NULL pointer here, if no message text is
                        supplied, but it is not recommended that you
                        should save messages with no text.

         Tagline      - unsigned char pointer to the TEAR line text, as
                        MsgControl allows you to define your own. This should
                        be NULL if you want the default tag -
                           '--- Zeus $(VER)'
                        The tagline should be in the format
                           '--- $(PROGNAME) $(VER)'.
                        You can also use a ^A PID kludge for program
                        information.
         
         Origin - unsigned char pointer to the origin text, in
                  the format ' * Origin: $(TEXT) (n:net/node.p)'
                  and should not be longer than 80 chars.
                  If you want MsgControl to make up the origin for
                  you as per the user's settings, then set this to
                  NULL.

         TextLength - Length of Message Text, excluding NULL (strlen()).

         TaglineLength - Length of user-supplied Tagline,
                         excluding NULL or 0 if you are using
                         the default MsgControl Tag.

         OriginLength - Length of user-supplied Origin,
                        excluding NULL or 0 if you are
                        using the default MsgControl Origins.

   RESULTS
    >0 - Number Message was Saved As.
          0 - Out of Memory.
         -1 - No Such Message Area.
         -2 - Can't allocate Full Message Text.
         -3 - Can't open Msg Description File.
         -4 - Can't open Msg Data File.
         -5 - Can't Open Pointer File
         -6 - Can't Read Pointer File
         -7 - Can't lock Pointer File.

   BUGS

   SEE ALSO
         ExampleSource/writemsg.c

@EndNode

