@Node ScanMessages()

zmf.library/ScanMessages

   NAME
      ScanMessages

   SYNOPSIS
      ULONG ScanMessages ( APTR, struct WholeMessage * )
       d0                   a0    a1
      res = ScanMessages ( Key, Message )

   FUNCTION
      Gets the next message in a message base. Use InitMsgScanKey ()
      before calling this function.

   INPUTS
      Key -- Key returned by InitMsgScanKey()
      Message -- An Allocated WholeMessage structure. The field
                 Message->wm_Text will be allocated by ScanMessages.
                 This must be freed by you afterwards.

   EXAMPLE
      ------------
      APTR                     Key
      struct   ScanInfo         si;
      struct   WholeMessage   msg;

      si.ScanFlag = 0;
      si.StartNumber = 0;
      si.Direction = SA_FORWARDS;
      si.Buffer = 32;
      si.Area = 1;

      Key = InitMsgScanKey ( &si ) ;
      if ( Key )
      {
         while ( ScanMessages ( Key, &msg ) )
         {
            /* Use Msg */
            FreeMem ( msg.wm_Text, msg.wm_TextLength ) ;
         }
         CloseMsgScanKey ( Key ) ;
      }

      ------------

   BUGS

@EndNode

@Node ScanMsgHdrs()

zmf.library/ScanMsgHdrs

   NAME
      ScanMsgHdrs

   SYNOPSIS
      ULONG ScanMsgHdrs ( APTR, struct Msg * )
       d0                   a0    a1
      res = ScanMessages ( Key, Msg )

   FUNCTION
      Gets the headers of the next message in a message base. Use
      InitMsgScanKey() before calling this function. Usage is simlar
      to ScanMessages() but the structure filled is Msg, rather than
      WholeMessage.

   INPUTS
      Key -- Key returned by InitMsgScanKey()
      Msg -- An allocated Msg structure which will be populated by
             this function.

   EXAMPLE
      ------------
      APTR                      Key
      struct   ScanInfo         si;
      struct   Msg              msg;

      si.ScanFlag = 0;
      si.StartNumber = 0;
      si.Direction = SA_FORWARDS;
      si.Buffer = 32;
      si.Area = 1;

      Key = InitMsgScanKey ( &si ) ;
      if ( Key )
      {
         while ( ScanMsgHdrs( Key, &msg ) )
         {
            /* Use Msg */
         }
         CloseMsgScanKey ( Key ) ;
      }

      ------------

   BUGS

@EndNode


@Node EditMessage()

zmf.library/EditMessage

    NAME
      EditFile

    SYNOPSIS
      signed int ( struct Msg *EditMessage, UBYTE *Text )
       d0           a0                       a1

    FUNCTION
      Edit's a message record, and the corresponding text. 

    INPUTS
      EditFile - Fully Completed record of message to edit. Unless you know
                  exactly what you are doing, I would recommend you do
                  not change the 'TextPosition' or 'TextLength' fields.
                  EditFile will do this for you.

      Text - New text for message, or NULL if the file description is
              to stay unchanged.

    RESULTS
      1 - Successful!
      0 - MsgControl not Running!
      -1- Bad Args!
      -2- Cannot open Text File
      -3- Cannot write new Text
      -4- Cannot find Message Record
      -5- Cannot write new Record
      -6- Cannot get Message Pointers

    NOTES
      There isn't any error checking, and it will write out whatever you
       specify in 'EditMessage', so be careful. If you are deleting the
       message, use DeleteMessage instead.


@EndNode

